  "knowledge": {
    "glossary": [
      {
        "term": "3W",
        "definition": "Who does what where: one row per organization, activity and admin area, with dates. An admin area with no row is a gap or a reporting failure, not proof of no work."
      },
      {
        "term": "Cluster",
        "definition": "A sector coordination group (health, water sanitation and hygiene, shelter, food security, protection, logistics and others) led by a cluster lead agency under the Humanitarian Coordinator."
      },
      {
        "term": "Humanitarian Country Team (HCT)",
        "definition": "The Humanitarian Coordinator with UN agencies, NGOs and the Red Cross and Red Crescent movement; agrees strategy, priorities, access and security approaches."
      },
      {
        "term": "Saving Lives Together",
        "definition": "The IASC framework for UN and NGO security collaboration (2015): sharing incident reports and alerts. It does not make the UN responsible for an NGO's security."
      },
      {
        "term": "Hibernation, relocation, evacuation",
        "definition": "Staying in a secure place; moving staff within the country; leaving the country. Three different decisions with different owners."
      }
    ],
    "productConventions": [
      "A flash update is numbered and dated, with sections: situation, humanitarian impact, response, gaps, access, contact. Say what is confirmed and what is an estimate.",
      "A gap list line names the sector, the area, the need, the owner and a date; an unassigned line says so."
    ],
    "realismRules": [
      "Cluster activation is requested by the Humanitarian Coordinator and decided by the Emergency Relief Coordinator with IASC Principals' endorsement; it is time-limited (IASC Transformative Agenda). Refugee settings use the refugee coordination model, not clusters (IASC and UNHCR, checked 2026-11-05).",
      "Name cluster lead agencies only when the scenario states them. The humanitarian principles are humanity, neutrality, impartiality and independence (UN General Assembly resolutions 46/182 and 58/114).",
      "Numbers agree across the flash update, the 3W table and the gap list. Days of stock equal stock on hand divided by daily consumption.",
      "Keep staff security and kidnapping content to decisions and communications: no negotiation tactics, ransom mechanics or detention-resistance technique."
    ]
  },
